                <pb facs="0430" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.20/170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-03T20:00:00-04:00">November 3, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>312. Department’s 216, October 31, 5 p.m. Minister of Foreign Affairs informed me
                    this afternoon that Cabinet had decided on immediate cancellation of contract of
                    Italian military mission but that Minister of War desired to retain three
                    members of it on new private contracts to continue teaching mapping, drawing, et
                    cetera, in staff college at Cochabamba as there were no substitutes available.
                    He <pb facs="0431" n="421" xml:id="pg421"/> promised me details as to names of
                    men, subjects taught and proposed lengths of contracts which will be forwarded
                    when received. I feel that retention of any members of Italian military mission
                    in whatever capacity is objectionable and respectfully recommend that the
                    Department insist on Bolivian Government’s keeping fully to its commitment. It
                    might be possible for substitute instructors to be furnished by the United
                    States Army as an additional military mission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
